# What a clone should NOT carry.
#
# Everything here is either regenerable, someone else's, or the user's
# own. Nothing in this file is deleted from a working tree; it is only
# kept out of the repository.

# Build output. `build-*` covers the trees the packaging scripts make
# (build-appimage), and cmake -B accepts any name, so the common ones are
# spelled out too.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# Staging directories the packaging steps write next to the source, both
# here and in CI.
install-tree/
deb-tree/
/out/
/dist/
.ccache/
# ctest's own scratch, if a build is ever configured in the source tree.
/Testing/

# What the AppImage build lays out and packs. Both normally live inside a
# build tree and are covered above; these catch a run pointed at the
# source directory instead.
/AppDir/
/packages/

# Python leftovers from tests/fixtures/make_toy_apk.py and anything a
# contributor runs beside it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Third-party dependencies fetched by tools/setup.sh: the Android NDK,
# the ANGLE build, and a real extracted bionic. None of them are Stud's
# and none of them are redistributable from here.
third_party/*
# AMD's FSR1 headers are the exception: a few KB, MIT licensed, and the
# reference render-host/shaders/upscale.comp is ported from. Keeping them
# out of the tree would leave that shader with nothing to be checked
# against, which is how its first version came to be wrong.
!third_party/fidelityfx-fsr1/
# And Qualcomm's SGSR1, for exactly the same reason: render-host/shaders/
# sgsr.comp is a port of it, and a port with no reference in the tree is
# how the EASU shader's first version came to be wrong. A few KB,
# BSD-3-Clause, and the licence has to travel with it.
!third_party/snapdragon-gsr/
# Same reasoning for the one vendored Wayland protocol: pointer-warp-v1 is
# staging and young enough that a distribution a release behind does not
# ship it, and a build should not fail over how new the host happens to
# be. 3.5 KB, MIT, and the system copy still wins when it exists.
!third_party/wayland-protocols/

# The real Roblox APK is user-supplied and must never be distributed.
# Stud does not ship, mirror or download it.
*.apk
*.apkm
*.apks
*.xapk

# Packages, built from this tree by cpack and packaging/build-appimage.sh.
# They belong on a release page, never in the history.
*.AppImage
*.AppImage.zsync
*.rpm
*.deb
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zsync

# Anything a run produces.
#
# Session logs live under ~/.local/state/stud/logs and the tray exports
# them as a tarball (covered above), but both end up in a repository the
# moment someone saves one here while reporting a problem.
*.log
# Frame dumps written by STUD_DUMP_FRAME.
*.ppm
# Crash dumps, and what perf leaves behind.
/core
core.[0-9]*
perf.data
perf.data.old

# Editor and tooling state. compile_commands.json is generated by cmake
# and usually symlinked to the root; .cache/ is clangd's index.
compile_commands.json
.cache/
CMakeUserPresets.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Merge and patch leftovers.
*.orig
*.rej

# Agent/working notes kept alongside the checkout, not part of the project.
# README-ref.md is the reference this README's layout was based on; it
# belongs to another project and stays out of this one.
README-ref.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
